Cross-job transport disposition
- All eight routes are subscription CLI routes. API-key credentials, provider SDKs, direct model HTTP endpoints, custom endpoints, driver substitution, and fallback are denied.
- Claude CLI schemas are deterministic inline projections that strip $schema and reject external $ref. Canonical schemas remain unchanged and are used again for output validation before admission.
- Claude receives the JSON document {instruction, authorized_input_projection} on stdin. It never relies on a staged path read while tools are closed.
- Claude capability closure is observed from stream-json initialization tools/MCP lists; Codex closure and identity are observed from its JSONL events. Claims never exceed observed evidence.
- Every staged input is hash/schema checked before transmission. Every returned document is validated against the unmodified canonical schema before admission.
- The N20 exact suite passed 508 tests plus 140 subtests (one intentional skip), and the graph-scoped provider/credential scan inspected 35 files with zero violations.
